    <briefdescription>
<para>Finite-differences pricing engine for dividend options using escowed dividends model. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The Merton-73 engine is the classic engine described in most derivatives texts. However, Haug, Haug, and Lewis in &quot;Back to
       Basics: a new approach to the discrete dividend problem&quot; argues that this scheme underprices call options. This is set as the default engine, because it is consistent with the analytic version. </para>    </detaileddescription>
